WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.201
Endpoints generate valuable telemetry about activity occurring on workstations, servers,

00:00:04.201 --> 00:00:05.842
and other managed devices.

00:00:05.842 --> 00:00:11.174
Depending on the platform and tools in use, events may describe process execution,

00:00:11.174 --> 00:00:14.865
command activity, file changes, registry modifications, user sessions, services,

00:00:14.865 --> 00:00:16.916
scheduled tasks, and network connections.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:20.607
Process telemetry can help analysts understand which program started,

00:00:20.607 --> 00:00:25.119
which user or parent process initiated it, what arguments were supplied,

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:26.759
and what happened next.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:30.861
File and configuration events can reveal changes to important locations,

00:00:30.861 --> 00:00:33.732
persistence mechanisms, security settings, or application state.

00:00:33.732 --> 00:00:38.653
Endpoint telemetry frequently plays a central role in investigations because it connects

00:00:38.653 --> 00:00:40.704
user activity with system behavior.

00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:45.215
Analysts may use it to establish a timeline, identify related hosts,

00:00:45.215 --> 00:00:48.086
verify whether a control blocked an action,

00:00:48.086 --> 00:00:52.188
or determine whether suspicious behavior continued after an initial event.

00:00:52.188 --> 00:00:53.828
Coverage still requires care.

00:00:53.828 --> 00:00:58.750
Devices may be offline, unmanaged, misconfigured, or unable to retain detailed events.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.852
Teams should monitor sensor health, collection policy, time synchronization, parsing,

00:01:02.852 --> 00:01:07.773
and gaps so that endpoint visibility remains dependable when an incident occurs.

00:01:07.773 --> 00:01:12.285
Collection settings should be tested against performance, privacy, and operational needs.

00:01:12.285 --> 00:01:17.206
Detailed endpoint data can be valuable, but excessive collection may increase storage,

00:01:17.206 --> 00:01:18.847
processing, or review costs.

00:01:18.847 --> 00:01:21.718
Teams should protect sensitive fields, restrict access,

00:01:21.718 --> 00:01:26.230
and document why higher-detail telemetry is necessary for particular assets, threats,

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.460
or response requirements.
